IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Code of the District of Columbia, Title 4, Chapter 2 (Public Assistance) -- Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF):
-- "earned income", "gross income" and "income" (s 4-205.05); residence (s 4-205.03); the gross income test (s 4-205.10); the
-- need determination and its disregards (s 4-205.11); the 60-month limit on federally funded TANF and its exemptions
-- (s 4-205.11a); the absent child and the 5-day notice (s 4-205.18(d)); the 45 days to decide an application (s 4-205.26); the
-- $10 floor (s 4-205.51); the payment and the standards of assistance (s 4-205.52); the duty to report changes (s 4-205.53(a));
-- notice of adverse action (s 4-205.55), the 15 days to answer information from another source (ss 4-205.56, 4-205.57),
-- benefits while a hearing is pending (s 4-205.59); and the 90 days to ask for a hearing and the hearing within 45 days
-- (s 4-210.09).
--
-- SEAT: the applicant for, or recipient of, TANF (the parent or caretaker). "Is our income low enough? How much would we get?
-- How long can we get it? How long can the agency take? What must I report, and by when? The agency says it will cut my
-- benefit: was the notice in time, will payments continue if I ask for a hearing, and by when must I ask?"
-- The Mayor (the Department of Human Services) appears only as what the Mayor must or may do to the family.
--
-- Edition: Code of the District of Columbia "through 2026-09-26" (last codified D.C. Law 26-187), from the Council's bulk XML
-- (github.com/DCCouncil/law-xml-codified, branch publication/2026-05-23, commit 9c950ac5), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/dc-code-4-ch2-subch-v-xxi-public-assistance-programs-2026-10.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19).
-- Not for model training (the Council's robots.txt signals ai-train=no).
--
-- INPUTS, not in the deposited text: the work-related expense deduction, the maximum child care deduction and the earned
-- income disregard, which s 4-205.11(a)(1), (2), (4A) leave to the Mayor's rules (DCMR, not deposited); the current level of
-- assistance, which s 4-205.52(d-1) raises each year for inflation from the 1998 table (the table is the default).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: POWER, GAC, GPA and the other categories; stepparent, parent and alien-sponsor deeming (ss 4-205.11(b),
-- 4-205.22); the assistance unit rules (s 4-205.15: the family size is an input); work requirements and sanctions
-- (ss 4-205.19b to 4-205.19h; only the 6% cap of s 4-205.18(e) is noted); lump sums (s 4-205.33); resources; the provisions
-- printed "[Applicable on October 1, 2026.]" without text (ss 4-205.11a(a-1), (g), 4-205.52(c-4): NOTES.md finding 1).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `District of Columbia TANF`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the s 4-205.52(c) table stops at a family of 19`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 4-205.52(c) -- the standards of assistance`

-- s 4-205.52(c): "The standards of assistance are set forth in the following table ...: Family Size | Standard Payment Level |
-- Level of Assistance". Read: the "Standard Payment Level" is the standard of assistance the tests compare income with
-- (ss 4-205.10, 4-205.11(a)(3)); the "Level of Assistance" is the "current payment level" a payment is worked from
-- (s 4-205.52(a)), the figure (d-1) raises for inflation (NOTES.md finding 2).
DECLARE `DC standards` HAS
    `standard payment level` IS A NUMBER
    `level of assistance`    IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the family size` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` `DC standards`
`the s 4-205.52(c) standards for` `the family size` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the family size` AT MOST 1  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 450, 239)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 2   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 560, 298)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 3   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 712, 379)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 4   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 870, 463)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 5   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 1002, 533)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 6   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 1178, 627)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 7   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 1352, 719)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 8   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 1494, 795)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 9   THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 1642, 874)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 10  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 1786, 950)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 11  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 1884, 1002)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 12  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2024, 1077)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 13  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2116, 1126)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 14  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2232, 1187)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 15  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2316, 1232)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 16  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2432, 1294)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 17  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2668, 1419)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 18  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2730, 1452)
        IF `the family size` EQUALS 19  THEN `answered` (`DC standards` OF 2786, 1482)
        OTHERWISE `not covered` `the s 4-205.52(c) table stops at a family of 19`

§§ `ss 4-205.05, 4-205.10, 4-205.11 -- income`

-- s 4-205.05(3): "'Gross income' means total earned income before any deductions required by law." (1): earned income "shall not
-- include the amount of earned income credit or other refundable income tax credit payments actually received". (4):
-- "income" includes earnings, benefits, pensions, unemployment and workers' compensation, child support, and more.
DECLARE `DC family month` HAS
    `family size`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `an initial applicant`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `earned income of adults`                            IS A NUMBER
    `earned income of children who are students`         IS A NUMBER  -- s 4-205.11(a)(4)
    `unearned income other than child support`           IS A NUMBER
    `child support received`                             IS A NUMBER
    `month is on or after 1 October 2025`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `work-related expense deduction set by rule`         IS A NUMBER  -- s 4-205.11(a)(1); input
    `child or incapacitated adult care paid, up to the maximum set by rule` IS A NUMBER  -- s 4-205.11(a)(2); input
    `earned income disregard set by rule`                IS A NUMBER  -- s 4-205.11(a)(4A); input
    `earned income disregards withheld under s 4-205.11(a)(6) or s 4-205.54(e)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4-205.10(a): "When the gross income of family applying for, or receiving TANF exceeds 100% of the standard of assistance
-- for a family of the same composition, as set forth in § 4-205.52, the family is not eligible for assistance." With
-- s 4-205.05(3), the gross income tested is earned income only (NOTES.md finding 3). Earnings of student children are counted
-- here: s 4-205.11(a)(4) disregards them in the need determination, after this test.
GIVEN `f` IS A `DC family month`
      `s` IS A `DC standards`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family passes the s 4-205.10 gross income test` IF
    (`f`'s `earned income of adults` PLUS `f`'s `earned income of children who are students`) AT MOST `s`'s `standard payment level`

-- s 4-205.11(a)(8): "Beginning on October 1, 2005, disregard up to the first $150 received per month by the assistance unit that
-- represents a current monthly child support obligation or a voluntary child support payment ..., and beginning on October 1,
-- 2025, disregard the full current monthly child support obligations and voluntary child support payments".
GIVEN `f` IS A `DC family month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the child support counted for` `f` MEANS
    IF   `f`'s `month is on or after 1 October 2025`
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (`f`'s `child support received` MINUS 150)

-- s 4-205.11(a)(1), (2): the work-related expense and the care deduction. (a)(3): "For initial applicants, determine whether the
-- monthly income, after disregards allowed under paragraph (1) or (2) ..., exceeds the standard of assistance. If so, the family
-- is ineligible for assistance."
GIVEN `f` IS A `DC family month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income after the (a)(1) and (a)(2) deductions of` `f` MEANS
        max 0 (   `f`'s `earned income of adults`
               MINUS `f`'s `work-related expense deduction set by rule`
               MINUS `f`'s `child or incapacitated adult care paid, up to the maximum set by rule`)
    PLUS `f`'s `unearned income other than child support`
    PLUS `the child support counted for` `f`

GIVEN `f` IS A `DC family month`
      `s` IS A `DC standards`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family passes the s 4-205.11(a)(3) applicant test` IF
    IF   `f`'s `an initial applicant`
    THEN `the income after the (a)(1) and (a)(2) deductions of` `f` AT MOST `s`'s `standard payment level`
    ELSE TRUE

-- The income the payment is worked from: (a)(1), (2), (4) (student children's earnings are left out), (4A) (the earned income
-- disregard), (8). (6) and s 4-205.54(e): in a month where the disregards are withheld (a job quit without good cause, a
-- late periodic report, and so on), the adults' earned income is counted with none of them.
GIVEN `f` IS A `DC family month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the countable income of` `f` MEANS
    `the countable earnings` PLUS `f`'s `unearned income other than child support` PLUS `the child support counted for` `f`
    WHERE
        `the countable earnings` MEANS
            IF   `f`'s `earned income disregards withheld under s 4-205.11(a)(6) or s 4-205.54(e)`
            THEN `f`'s `earned income of adults`
            ELSE max 0 (   `f`'s `earned income of adults`
                        MINUS `f`'s `work-related expense deduction set by rule`
                        MINUS `f`'s `child or incapacitated adult care paid, up to the maximum set by rule`
                        MINUS `f`'s `earned income disregard set by rule`)

§§ `s 4-205.52(a), s 4-205.51 -- the payment`

-- s 4-205.52(a): "the Mayor shall subtract any income of the assistance unit, after applicable disregards, from the current
-- payment level for a family that is the size of the assistance unit." s 4-205.51: "No assistance unit will receive TANF
-- monthly benefits if the benefit check prior to adjustments is less than $10."
GIVEN `f` IS A `DC family month`
      `s` IS A `DC standards`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the TANF payment for` `f` `with standards` `s` MEANS
    IF       `the family passes the s 4-205.10 gross income test` `f` `s`
         AND `the family passes the s 4-205.11(a)(3) applicant test` `f` `s`
         AND `the check` AT LEAST 10
    THEN `the check`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the check` MEANS max 0 (`s`'s `level of assistance` MINUS `the countable income of` `f`)

§§ `s 4-205.11a -- the 60-month limit`

-- (a): "Federally-funded TANF benefits shall not be provided to any assistance unit that includes an adult who has received
-- federally-funded TANF benefits for 60 months (whether or not consecutive) after February 28, 1997." (b): months as a minor
-- child who was not the head of the unit or married to the head are not counted; (c): months with no check because it would
-- have been under $10 are not counted; (d): months in Indian country or an Alaskan Native village with 50% or more of adults
-- not employed are not counted. (e): "The Mayor may exempt an assistance unit ... by reason of hardship or if the assistance
-- unit includes an individual who has been battered or subject to extreme cruelty" (a judgment: answered conditionally).
DECLARE `What the 60-month limit means for us` IS ONE OF
    `federally funded TANF may continue: fewer than 60 counted months`
    `federally funded TANF may continue only if the Mayor exempts the unit for hardship or battering or extreme cruelty (s 4-205.11a(e))`

GIVEN `counted months of federally funded TANF of the adult with the most` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What the 60-month limit means for us`
`the s 4-205.11a answer for` `counted months of federally funded TANF of the adult with the most` MEANS
    IF   `counted months of federally funded TANF of the adult with the most` LESS THAN 60
    THEN `federally funded TANF may continue: fewer than 60 counted months`
    ELSE `federally funded TANF may continue only if the Mayor exempts the unit for hardship or battering or extreme cruelty (s 4-205.11a(e))`

§§ `Duties, notices and hearings`

DECLARE `DC TANF party` IS ONE OF
    `the Mayor`
    `the recipient`
    `the parent, guardian or caretaker`

DECLARE `DC TANF action` IS ONE OF
    `approve or disapprove the application`
    `notify the Mayor of the change`
    `notify the Mayor of the child's absence`
    `present additional information or request a fair hearing`

-- s 4-205.26: "Such action shall be taken on applications for public assistance not in excess of 45 days ... from the date the
-- application is received to the date the applicant receives his 1st assistance payment ... or a notice of ineligibility,
-- unless a delay is caused by unusual circumstance beyond the Mayor's control" (the applicant's own doing, hospitalization or
-- imprisonment, an emergency). s 4-205.27: the Mayor "shall not terminate his consideration of an application ... solely
-- because he has been unable to establish the eligibility of the applicant within the 45- or 60-day period."
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DC TANF party` `DC TANF action`
`the 45 days to decide an application` MEANS
    PARTY  `the Mayor`
    MUST   `approve or disapprove the application`
    WITHIN 45
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the Mayor` BECAUSE "no first payment or notice of ineligibility within 45 days of receipt (s 4-205.26), unless an unusual circumstance beyond the Mayor's control caused the delay; the application stays open (s 4-205.27)"

-- s 4-205.53(a): "it shall be the recipient's duty to notify the Mayor of this information immediately upon the receipt or
-- possession of the additional resources, or upon the change in circumstances. A recipient shall inform the Mayor whenever the
-- recipient begins to receive earned income ... and whenever the recipient ceases to receive earned income." "Immediately"
-- has no number, so the rule has no WITHIN.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DC TANF party` `DC TANF action`
`the duty to report a change immediately` MEANS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    MUST   `notify the Mayor of the change`
    HENCE  FULFILLED

-- s 4-205.18(d)(2): "A parent, guardian, or other caretaker of a minor child shall be determined ineligible to receive TANF
-- benefits if the parent, guardian, or caretaker fails to notify the Mayor of the absence of the child from the home after the
-- 5-day period beginning with the date on which it becomes clear ... that the child will be absent from the home for more than
-- 90 consecutive days." Days from the day it becomes clear: the five days are day 0 to day 4.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DC TANF party` `DC TANF action`
`the 5 days to report a child's long absence` MEANS
    PARTY  `the parent, guardian or caretaker`
    MUST   `notify the Mayor of the child's absence`
    WITHIN 4
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the parent, guardian or caretaker` BECAUSE "the child's absence of more than 90 days not reported within the 5-day period: the parent, guardian or caretaker is ineligible for TANF (s 4-205.18(d)(2))"

-- ss 4-205.56(a), 4-205.57: where the information for a cut comes from someone else, the recipient "has 15 days to present
-- additional information, or, in lieu thereof, to request a fair hearing"; if not, after 15 days from the postmark "the
-- representative of the Mayor shall take immediate action to reduce or terminate the assistance payment". Not answering is no
-- breach by the recipient: its consequence is the cut.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `DC TANF party` `DC TANF action`
`the 15 days to answer information from another source` MEANS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    DO     `present additional information or request a fair hearing`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   FULFILLED

-- s 4-205.55(a)(1): "'Timely' means that the notice is postmarked at least 15 days before the date upon which the action would
-- become effective". (b) lists five cases where timely notice may be dispensed with.
GIVEN `the postmark` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
      `one of the s 4-205.55(b) cases applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice of the adverse action was timely` IF
        `one of the s 4-205.55(b) cases applies`
    OR  Day `the effective date` MINUS Day `the postmark` AT LEAST 15

-- s 4-205.59(a): "If the recipient requests a hearing before the date that the termination, suspension, or reduction of aid is to
-- become effective, assistance shall not be discontinued ..." until the request is withdrawn or decided. (c): where the action
-- was taken without the timely notice the law requires and the hearing is requested "within 10 days of the postmark", "the
-- Mayor shall reinstate assistance within 96 hours". (d): a later request within s 4-210.09 is honoured "but shall not result
-- in the continuation of disputed benefits".
DECLARE `My benefits while the hearing is pending` IS ONE OF
    `assistance continues unchanged until the hearing decision (s 4-205.59(a))`
    `assistance must be reinstated within 96 hours of my request (s 4-205.59(c))`
    `the hearing is held, but the disputed benefits do not continue (s 4-205.59(d))`

GIVEN `the postmark` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
      `the notice was timely` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I request a hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `My benefits while the hearing is pending`
`the s 4-205.59 answer for` `the postmark` `the effective date` `the notice was timely` `the day I request a hearing` MEANS
    IF   `the day I request a hearing` LESS THAN `the effective date`
    THEN `assistance continues unchanged until the hearing decision (s 4-205.59(a))`
    ELSE IF   (NOT `the notice was timely`) AND Day `the day I request a hearing` MINUS Day `the postmark` AT MOST 10
         THEN `assistance must be reinstated within 96 hours of my request (s 4-205.59(c))`
         ELSE `the hearing is held, but the disputed benefits do not continue (s 4-205.59(d))`

§ `Questions for the applicant or recipient`

§§ `The standards`

@export What are the District's TANF standards of assistance for a family of this size, as printed in s 4-205.52(c) (the 1998 table)?
GIVEN `my family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TANF assistance unit
GIVETH AN `Answer` `DC standards`
`What are the DC TANF standards for my family` MEANS `the s 4-205.52(c) standards for` `my family size`

§§ `How much?`

@export How much TANF would my family get this month (s 4-205.52(a))? The deductions and the current level of assistance come from the Mayor's rules.
GIVEN `my family size` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your TANF assistance unit (1 to 19)
      `we are applying for the first time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an initial applicant (not already receiving TANF)
      `adults' earnings this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Earned income of the adults this month before deductions, in US dollars (not EITC or other refundable tax credits)
      `student children's earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Earnings this month of children receiving TANF who are full-time students, or part-time students not working full time, in US dollars
      `other income this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Unearned income other than child support (benefits, pensions, unemployment or workers' compensation, interest), in US dollars
      `child support this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Current or voluntary child support received this month, in US dollars
      `the month is October 2025 or later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the month is October 2025 or later (child support is then fully disregarded)
      `the work expense deduction` IS A NUMBER @desc The work-related expense deduction under the Mayor's rules, in US dollars (0 if no earnings)
      `my care costs, up to the rule's maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc What you pay for care of your children or an incapacitated adult, up to the maximum in the Mayor's rules, in US dollars
      `the earned income disregard` IS A NUMBER @desc The earned income disregard under the Mayor's rules for this month, in US dollars
      `my disregards are withheld this month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agency withholds your earned income disregards this month (for example a job quit without good cause, or a late periodic report)
      `the current level of assistance` IS A NUMBER @desc The current level of assistance for your family size as adjusted for inflation; leave 0 to use the 1998 figure in s 4-205.52(c)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`How much DC TANF would we get` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 4-205.52(c) standards for` `my family size`
    WHEN `not covered` `the gap` THEN `not covered` `the gap`
    WHEN `answered` `the table` THEN
        `answered` (`the TANF payment for` `the family` `with standards` (`DC standards` OF (`the table`'s `standard payment level`), `the level`))
        WHERE
            `the level` MEANS
                IF `the current level of assistance` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the current level of assistance` ELSE `the table`'s `level of assistance`
            `the family` MEANS
                `DC family month` OF `my family size`, `we are applying for the first time`, `adults' earnings this month`,
                                     `student children's earnings`, `other income this month`, `child support this month`,
                                     `the month is October 2025 or later`, `the work expense deduction`,
                                     `my care costs, up to the rule's maximum`, `the earned income disregard`,
                                     `my disregards are withheld this month`

@export Can my family keep getting federally funded TANF under the 60-month limit (s 4-205.11a)?
GIVEN `counted months` IS A NUMBER @desc The most months of federally funded TANF any adult in your unit has received since March 1997, leaving out months as a minor child (not head of the unit or married to the head), months with no check because it would have been under $10, and months in Indian country or an Alaskan Native village with high non-employment
GIVETH A `What the 60-month limit means for us`
`Can we keep getting federally funded TANF` MEANS `the s 4-205.11a answer for` `counted months`

§§ `Deadlines`

@export By what date must the agency act on my TANF application (s 4-205.26)?
GIVEN `the day the application was received` IS A DATE @desc The date the Department received your application
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the agency act on my application` MEANS `the day the application was received` PLUS 45

@export By what date must I tell the agency that my child will be away from home for more than 90 days (s 4-205.18(d)(2))?
GIVEN `the day it became clear` IS A DATE @desc The day it became clear to you that your child will be absent from the home for more than 90 consecutive days
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report my child's absence` MEANS `the day it became clear` PLUS 4

@export The agency told me it will cut, stop or change my TANF: was the notice timely (s 4-205.55(a))?
GIVEN `the postmark of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The postmark date on the agency's notice
      `the date the action takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The date the cut, stop or change is to take effect
      `one of the exceptions applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the s 4-205.55(b) cases applies: your written request to stop, a death, unknown whereabouts, assistance granted elsewhere, or a special allowance ending as you were told
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the notice timely` IF
    `the notice of the adverse action was timely` `the postmark of the notice` `the date the action takes effect` `one of the exceptions applies`

@export If I ask for a hearing on a cut, stop or change, will my TANF continue meanwhile (s 4-205.59)?
GIVEN `the postmark of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The postmark date on the agency's notice of the action
      `the date the action takes effect` IS A DATE @desc The date the action takes (or took) effect
      `the notice was timely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the notice was timely (postmarked at least 15 days before the action, unless an exception applies)
      `the day I ask for a hearing` IS A DATE @desc The day you request the hearing
GIVETH A `My benefits while the hearing is pending`
`Will my TANF continue during the hearing` MEANS
    `the s 4-205.59 answer for` `the postmark of the notice` `the date the action takes effect` `the notice was timely` `the day I ask for a hearing`

@export Until what date may I ask for a fair hearing on an adverse TANF action (s 4-210.09)?
GIVEN `the postmark of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The postmark date on the agency's notice of the adverse action and of your right to a hearing
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when may I ask for a hearing` MEANS `the postmark of the notice` PLUS 90
